# Manual setup steps: things no script can do (privacy permissions, sign-ins, MDM
# apps, settings that aren't exposed via `defaults`). This file is the single source
# of truth for them. It is read by:
#   scripts/manual-steps.sh list | open | check   (numbered checklist, walk-through, checks)
#   install.sh / bootstrap.sh                      (print the checklist at the end)
#   macconfig-check.sh                                       ("Manual steps" section)
# docs/manual-steps.md is generated by scripts/render-manual-steps-doc.sh
# (the table is `scripts/manual-steps.sh list --markdown`).
#
# Format (pipe-delimited, one step per line):
#   id | group | title | where | open | check
#   id:    unique kebab-case id
#   group: heading the step is listed under (keep a group's steps together)
#   title: what to do, in plain English
#   where: where to do it (System Settings paths use macOS 27 names)
#   open:  what `manual-steps.sh open` opens, or empty:
#            x-apple.systempreferences:<pane>  a System Settings pane
#            https://… | macappstore://…   a web page / the App Store
#            app:<App Name>                 open -a "<App Name>"
#   check: how `manual-steps.sh check` verifies it (always read-only), or empty = check by hand:
#            tcc:<Service>:<bundle-id>      allowed in the system TCC database (kTCCService<Service>);
#                                           reading it needs Full Disk Access, else check by hand
#            defaults:<domain>:<k=v>[,k=v]  every key reads back as that value
#            app:<path>                     path exists (@HOME@ -> $HOME)
#            logi:<id>[,<id>]               Logi Options+ values match lib/logi-expected.list
#                                           (read from a temp copy of settings.db by
#                                           lib/logi-settings.py; never written)
#            @macconfig-check.sh                      verified by its own macconfig-check.sh section (not repeated here)
#            hammerspoon-ax | karabiner-driver | pointer-size | input-british | op-cli | gh-auth
#            | app-store | spotlight-results
#                                           named checks. pointer-size, input-british, op-cli,
#                                           gh-auth, and app-store live in lib/session-checks.sh
#                                           (also the macconfig-check.sh section; warn only, never --fix).
#                                           spotlight-results is the same file. The toggles cannot
#                                           be read, so the result is check by hand, reported with
#                                           the other manual steps.
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored. Fields must not contain '|'.

# ---- Sign-ins ----
gh-auth|Sign-ins|Sign in to the GitHub CLI (needed to clone this private repo)|Terminal: gh auth login||gh-auth
apple-account|Sign-ins|Sign in with your Apple Account (your @icloud.com Apple ID)|System Settings → Apple Account|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.systempreferences.AppleIDSettings|
icloud-sync|Sign-ins|iCloud: Photos, iCloud Drive, Messages and other unused sync Off; Passwords (iCloud Keychain) and Find My On|System Settings → Apple Account → iCloud|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.systempreferences.AppleIDSettings|
app-store|Sign-ins|Sign in to the App Store (brew bundle needs it for WhatsApp and the other mas apps). macconfig checks this with mas list|App Store → Store → Sign In|macappstore://|app-store

# ---- Company apps (MDM) ----
mdm-apps|Company apps (MDM)|Install Okta Verify and 1Password from Iru Self Service (Kandji), not Homebrew|Applications → Iru Self Service|app:Iru Self Service|@macconfig-check.sh
1password-signin|Company apps (MDM)|Sign in to 1Password and unlock it|1Password app|app:1Password|
1password-cli|Company apps (MDM)|Turn on Integrate with 1Password CLI, then run op whoami in a terminal|1Password → Settings → Developer|app:1Password|op-cli

# ---- Apps not in the Brewfile ----
cursor-nightly|Apps not in the Brewfile|Install Cursor Nightly (separate app, next to the stable Cursor)|cursor.com/nightlydownload|https://cursor.com/nightlydownload|app:/Applications/Cursor Nightly.app
youtube-music|Apps not in the Brewfile|Install YouTube Music as a Chrome app|Chrome → music.youtube.com → ⋮ → Cast, save, and share → Install page as app|https://music.youtube.com|app:@HOME@/Applications/Chrome Apps.localized/YouTube Music.app

# ---- Privacy & Security permissions ----
hammerspoon-ax|Privacy & Security permissions|Allow Hammerspoon (Sidecar → Slack), then restart it and choose Reload Config|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Device Control and Data Access → Hammerspoon|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_Accessibility|hammerspoon-ax
karabiner-driver|Privacy & Security permissions|Enable the Karabiner DriverKit VirtualHIDDevice driver|System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions → Driver Extensions|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.LoginItems-Settings.extension|karabiner-driver
karabiner-ax|Privacy & Security permissions|Allow Karabiner-Elements and Karabiner-Core-Service|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Device Control and Data Access|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_Accessibility|tcc:Accessibility:org.pqrs.Karabiner-Core-Service
karabiner-login-items|Privacy & Security permissions|Allow Karabiner-Elements to run in the background (macconfig checks this: Karabiner-Core-Service and Karabiner-VirtualHIDDevice-Daemon are enabled and allowed). Karabiner-Elements Privileged Daemons v2 may stay disabled. macconfig does not change this|System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions → Allow in the Background|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.LoginItems-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh
raycast-ax|Privacy & Security permissions|Allow Raycast (needed for Clipboard History)|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Device Control and Data Access → Raycast|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_Accessibility|tcc:Accessibility:com.raycast.macos
ghostty-fda|Privacy & Security permissions|Give Ghostty Full Disk Access (lets macconfig-check.sh read Login Items and Finder Recents)|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access → Ghostty|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_AllFiles|tcc:SystemPolicyAllFiles:com.mitchellh.ghostty
grokbot-fda|Privacy & Security permissions|Give Grok Bot Full Disk Access (for its unattended macconfig-check.sh runs)|System Settings → Privacy & Security → Full Disk Access → Grok Bot|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_AllFiles|tcc:SystemPolicyAllFiles:com.anysphere.sand

# ---- Trackpad, mouse & pointer ----
# Tap to click, click pressure, secondary click, three-finger drag, tracking speed,
# and Force Click (On) are lib/macos-defaults.list. A change may need a logout/login.
# Look up & data detectors is NSGlobalDomain com.apple.trackpad.forceClick = 0.
# That is a check only. ActuateDetents and ForceSuppressed stay in the defaults
# list (Force Click and haptic feedback On) and are a different setting.
trackpad-lookup|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Trackpad: Look up & data detectors Off|System Settings → Trackpad → Point & Click|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Trackpad-Settings.extension|defaults:NSGlobalDomain:com.apple.trackpad.forceClick=0
# Dragging lives in Accessibility. defaults write of Dragging/DragLock does not reliably
# change that pane, so this stays a check only. Paul wants dragging On, without drag lock.
trackpad-dragging|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Use trackpad for dragging On (Without Drag Lock)|System Settings → Accessibility → Pointer Control → Trackpad Options|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Accessibility-Settings.extension|defaults:com.apple.AppleMultitouchTrackpad:Dragging=1,DragLock=0
pointer-size|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Pointer size one notch above Normal (macconfig checks this; set the slider by hand)|System Settings → Accessibility → Display → Pointer → Pointer size|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Accessibility-Settings.extension|pointer-size
# Tracking speed and scrolling speed are readable, but defaults write does not
# reliably drive System Settings → Mouse on recent macOS, so they stay a check
# only (warn on drift; macconfig-check.sh --fix does not write them). The
# double-click threshold key is unset on this Mac, and secondary click has no
# separate reliable key, so those two stay in the step text.
mouse-settings|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Mouse: tracking speed 1.5 and scrolling speed 0.5 (checked only; writing them is unreliable). Double-click speed faster and secondary click on the right side stay by hand (the double-click threshold key is unset). The wheel's direction, Natural, is set in Logi Options+ and checked by macconfig-check.sh|System Settings → Mouse|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Mouse-Settings.extension|defaults:NSGlobalDomain:com.apple.mouse.scaling=1.5,com.apple.scrollwheel.scaling=0.5
logi-smooth-scrolling|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Logi Options+: Smooth scrolling On (main wheel and thumb wheel)|Logi Options+ → MX Master 3S → Point & Scroll|app:logioptionsplus|logi:wheel-smooth,thumb-smooth
logi-cloud-backup|Trackpad, mouse & pointer|Logi Options+: sign in and turn on cloud backup (Automatically backup all devices); confirm it shows a recent Last backup|Logi Options+ → MX Master 3S → Settings → Other → Automatically backup all devices|app:logioptionsplus|

# ---- Display, keyboard & desktop ----
# More Space is _spdisplays_resolution starting with the value for this panel
# size in lib/display-resolution.list (14" 1800 x 1169, 16" 2056 x 1329).
# macconfig-check.sh reads system_profiler and never changes the mode. An
# unlisted panel size or a clamshell Mac (no built-in panel) is an info skip.
display-more-space|Display, keyboard & desktop|Built-in display: More Space (macconfig checks this from the display report; set it by hand)|System Settings → Displays|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Displays-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh
auto-brightness|Display, keyboard & desktop|Displays: Automatically adjust brightness Off (macconfig checks this; leave True Tone and Slightly dim the display on battery as they are)|System Settings → Displays|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Displays-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh
wallpaper|Display, keyboard & desktop|Wallpaper: Tahoe Night (Landscape). macconfig reads the wallpaper store and warns if it is a different picture. It does not change it|System Settings → Wallpaper|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Wallpaper-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh
# Mains power: sleep 0, display sleep 10 minutes, wake for network access on.
# Battery: display sleep 2 minutes. Battery idle sleep is not changed.
# Closing the lid still sleeps the Mac. The screen still locks.
# macconfig-check.sh reads `pmset -g custom` and warns. --fix does not run sudo.
# macos.sh may run the sudo pmset commands and skips them when sudo is not available.
ac-sleep|Display, keyboard & desktop|On mains power the Mac does not sleep on its own, the display sleeps after 10 minutes, and wake for network access is on. On battery the display sleeps after 2 minutes. Closing the lid still sleeps the Mac. Battery idle sleep is not changed|Terminal: sudo pmset -c sleep 0; sudo pmset -c displaysleep 10; sudo pmset -b displaysleep 2; sudo pmset -c womp 1||@macconfig-check.sh
input-british|Display, keyboard & desktop|Keyboard input source: British (macconfig checks the selected layout is British only)|System Settings → Keyboard → Text Input → Input Sources|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Keyboard-Settings.extension|input-british
# Desktop widgets and Stage Manager are lib/macos-defaults.list (StandardHideWidgets,
# StageManagerHideWidgets, GloballyEnabled). Click wallpaper to reveal desktop stays out.
user-picture|Display, keyboard & desktop|Set your user picture to the Dog (macconfig checks this). A different picture is a warning. macconfig does not change it|System Settings → Users & Groups → your account picture|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Users-Groups-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh

# ---- Notifications & Spotlight ----
notifications-mirroring|Notifications & Spotlight|Notifications Off when mirroring or sharing the display|System Settings → Notifications|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Notifications-Settings.extension|
# Bundle ids live in lib/notifications-off.list. macconfig-check.sh reads the
# usernoted plist and never writes it. Mirroring stays the row above.
notifications-apps|Notifications & Spotlight|Turn notifications Off for Calendar, Cursor Nightly, FaceTime, Game Center, Home, Mail, Microsoft Teams, Slack, Spotify, Tips, Wallet, Kandji, Tailscale, Logi Options+, Cog, Gemini, Grok Bot, ChatGPT, Multipass, Yubico Authenticator, YouTube Music, Sonos|System Settings → Notifications → Application Notifications|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Notifications-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh
spotlight-results|Notifications & Spotlight|Spotlight: turn off results from Books, Calendar, Contacts, Keynote, Mail, Messages, Music, Notes, Numbers, Photos, Podcasts, Reminders, Safari, Shortcuts, Stocks, Tips, and Voice Memos. Leave App Store, Calculator, Dictionary, System Settings, and WhatsApp on. Check this page by hand (macconfig cannot read the toggles)|System Settings → Spotlight → Results from Apps|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Spotlight-Settings.extension|spotlight-results

# ---- Login Items & Finder ----
login-items-off|Login Items & Finder|Keep ChatGPT, Gemini and GeminiAppLauncher Off at login|System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.LoginItems-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh
finder-sidebar|Login Items & Finder|Finder sidebar (macconfig checks this): the Tags group stays collapsed, Recents stays hidden, and, when the sidebar files name the row, Shared is the first visible row, AirDrop and iCloud Drive are hidden, and your home folder, Macintosh HD, Network, and Trash are visible. A row the files do not name stays by hand. macconfig does not change the sidebar|Finder → Settings → Sidebar|app:Finder|@macconfig-check.sh

# ---- App settings ----
gemini-shortcuts|App settings|Gemini shortcuts: Mini chat Control+Option+G, Full chat Control+Option+Shift+G (defaults clash with ChatGPT)|Gemini → Settings → Shortcuts|app:Gemini|
raycast-import|App settings|Raycast: on a new Mac, import your .rayconfig backup (tick Settings, Aliases & Hotkeys), or set the three Raycast items below by hand; keep Scheduled Backup on (never in this repo: it holds clipboard history and extension settings)|Raycast → Import Settings & Data (backups: Raycast → Settings → Advanced → Export / Scheduled Backup)|app:Raycast|
raycast-hotkey|App settings|Raycast hotkey: Shift+Control+Command+R (off Option+Space, which clashes with ChatGPT)|Raycast → Settings → General → Raycast Hotkey|app:Raycast|defaults:com.raycast.macos:raycastGlobalHotkey=Shift-Control-Command-15
raycast-finder-hotkey|App settings|Raycast: Finder hotkey Shift+Control+Command+F|Raycast → type Finder → Command+K → Configure Application… → Record Hotkey|app:Raycast|
raycast-clipboard|App settings|Raycast Clipboard History: hotkey Control+Command+V, keep history 1 day, disable 1Password and 1Password for Safari|Raycast → Settings → Extensions → Clipboard History|app:Raycast|

# ---- Modes (Hammerspoon menu-bar switcher; see docs/modes.md) ----
mode-focus-modes|Modes (menu-bar switcher)|Create two Focus modes named WebConf and DeepWork (WebConf: allow Granola; DeepWork: allow Hammerspoon, so the end-of-session notification gets through)|System Settings → Focus → Add Focus… → Custom|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Focus-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh
mode-focus-shortcuts|Modes (menu-bar switcher)|Create four Shortcuts, each with one Set Focus action: "Mode WebConf On" (Turn WebConf On until Turned Off), "Mode WebConf Off" (Turn WebConf Off), "Mode DeepWork On", "Mode DeepWork Off". Also create "Mode Upcoming Meetings". macconfig checks all five with shortcuts list|Shortcuts → + → search "Set Focus"|app:Shortcuts|@macconfig-check.sh
mode-hammerspoon-alerts|Modes (menu-bar switcher)|Hammerspoon notifications: style Alerts, so the DeepWork end-of-session buttons (Take a break / Back to Normal / Another session) show|System Settings → Notifications → Hammerspoon → Alerts|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.Notifications-Settings.extension|@macconfig-check.sh
mode-menubar-pin|Modes (menu-bar switcher)|Pin the mode-switcher menu-bar icon so it stays visible: hold Command (⌘) and drag it toward Control Centre / the clock, because icons further from them get auto-hidden behind <<|Menu bar → ⌘-drag the mode icon (desktop computer / red ⏺ / brain)||

# ---- Menu bar (third-party allow list) ----
# Raycast, Logi Options+ and Docker have no reliable defaults key for this toggle.
# Raycast's own menu-bar switch is not scriptable. Leave the other icons alone.
menubar-third-party-hide|Menu bar|Allow in the Menu Bar: turn Off Raycast, Logi Options+ and Docker. Leave Tailscale, 1Password, Granola, Hammerspoon and Kandji/company agents as they are. Raycast's own menu-bar toggle isn't scriptable|System Settings → Menu Bar → Allow in the Menu Bar|x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.ControlCenter-Settings.extension|
